# Supabase CLI scratch state lives in `supabase/.gitignore`, which is the
# CLI's own template -- `.branches` and `.temp` both belong to it.

# Claude Code. `.claude/skills/` IS tracked: those are repo-specific workflow
# definitions, the same category as CLAUDE.md. Everything below is per-machine
# state that would only conflict between developers, and `settings.local.json`
# additionally holds personal tool-permission grants.
#
# The directory as a whole is deliberately not ignored. Ignoring it would hide
# the tracked skills from `git status` when they change, and an unignored
# `.claude/` is also what made one of them visible enough to commit at all --
# it had otherwise sat untracked since it was written.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/state/

# Vendored agent skills, installed by `npx skills add`. The files live in
# `.agents/skills/` and `.claude/skills/` holds symlinks into it, so both sides
# are ignored -- committing them would vendor someone else's skill into this
# repo and shadow the identically-named plugin skill for everyone who clones it.
# The repo's own skills (hhvc-ship-workflow, verify) stay tracked.
.agents/
.claude/skills/supabase
.claude/skills/supabase-postgres-best-practices

# Sentry Config File
.env.sentry-build-plugin

# Design reference dropped in from the mockup tooling -- .dc.html artboards,
# exported zips, scratch notes. 8.5M of binaries that nothing in the app
# imports, so it is reference material a person opens, not source the build
# reads. The `:Zone.Identifier` files alongside them are Windows
# alternate-data-stream stubs that ride along when files cross from Windows
# into WSL; they are noise wherever they land -- hence the second pattern,
# which catches the ones that land outside `design/` too.
design/
*:Zone.Identifier
